Q: Bootstrap: Centering Elements Vertically and Horizontally A: <h3>Bootstrap 5.3.8 (Updated 2026)</h3>
<p>There are several suggestions involving bad practices, such as using pure CSS, a combination of Bootstrap classes with custom CSS, or even unnecessary Bootstrap classes.</p>
<p>Below, you can find the minimum required code to achieve the desired result <strong>natively</strong>, with an in-depth analysis for those seeking a better understanding.</p>
<h4>TL;DR:</h4>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.8/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css"
        rel="stylesheet"/&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;div class="vh-100 d-flex justify-content-center align-items-center"&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;This content is centered vertically and horizontally.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<hr />
<h3>In-depth explanation:</h3>
<ol>
<li><p><strong>vh-100:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> This class sets the height of the element to 100% of the <a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_rwd_viewport.asp" rel="nofollow noreferrer">viewport</a> height.</li>
<li><strong>Behind the scenes:</strong> Bootstrap applies the <code>height: 100vh;</code> CSS property, making the container take up the entire height of the viewport.</li>
<li><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="true" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code snippet-currently-hidden">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.8/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet"/&gt;
    &lt;style&gt;
        .outer-container {
            border: 2px solid red; 
        }
        .inner-content {
            border: 2px solid blue; 
        }
    &lt;/style&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
    &lt;div class="vh-100 outer-container"&gt;
        &lt;p class="inner-content"&gt;vh-100 applied.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><p><strong>d-flex:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> This class is used to enable the <a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css3_flexbox.asp" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Flexbox</a> layout for the container. Flexbox is a one-dimensional layout method for laying out items in rows or columns.</li>
<li><strong>Behind the scenes:</strong> Bootstrap applies the <code>display: flex;</code> CSS property to the element, making it a flex container. This allows you to use properties like <a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css3_flexbox_container.asp#justify-content" rel="nofollow noreferrer">justify-content</a> and <a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css3_flexbox_container.asp#align-items" rel="nofollow noreferrer">align-items</a> to control the alignment of its children.</li>
<li>More information about <code>display</code> property can be found <a href="https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/utilities/display/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">here</a>.</li>
<li><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="true" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code snippet-currently-hidden">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.8/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet"/&gt;
    &lt;style&gt;
        .outer-container {
            border: 2px solid red; 
        }
        .inner-content {
            border: 2px solid blue; 
        }
    &lt;/style&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
    &lt;div class="vh-100 d-flex outer-container"&gt;
        &lt;p class="inner-content"&gt;vh-100 and d-flex applied.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><p><strong>justify-content-center:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> This class is used to horizontally align the child elements (content) of the flex container to the center.</li>
<li><strong>Behind the scenes:</strong> Bootstrap applies the <code>justify-content: center;</code> CSS property to the flex container, ensuring its children are horizontally centered.</li>
<li><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="true" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code snippet-currently-hidden">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.8/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet"/&gt;
    &lt;style&gt;
        .outer-container {
            border: 2px solid red; 
        }
        .inner-content {
            border: 2px solid blue; 
        }
    &lt;/style&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
    &lt;div class="vh-100 d-flex justify-content-center outer-container"&gt;
        &lt;p class="inner-content"&gt;vh-100 and d-flex and justify-content-center applied.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><p><strong>align-items-center:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> This class is used to vertically align the child elements (content) of the flex container to the center.</li>
<li><strong>Behind the scenes:</strong> Bootstrap applies the <code>align-items: center;</code> CSS property to the flex container, ensuring its children are vertically centered.</li>
<li><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="true" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code snippet-currently-hidden">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.8/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet"/&gt;
    &lt;style&gt;
        .outer-container {
            border: 2px solid red; 
        }
        .inner-content {
            border: 2px solid blue; 
        }
    &lt;/style&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
    &lt;div class="vh-100 d-flex justify-content-center align-items-center outer-container"&gt;
        &lt;p class="inner-content"&gt;vh-100 and d-flex and justify-content-center and align-items-center applied.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
